{"question": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Lani baked 55 cookies. She ate 5 five cookies and placed the rest equally into five jars. How many cookies were in each jar?\n Solution:\n<think>\n", "gold_ans": "10", "rationale": "First, I need to determine how many cookies Lani ate. She ate 5 cookies five times, which totals 25 cookies.\n\nNext, I'll calculate the number of cookies she has left after eating. She baked a total of 55 cookies and ate 25, so 55 minus 25 equals 30 cookies remaining.\n\nFinally, to find out how many cookies are in each jar, I'll divide the remaining cookies by the number of jars. Dividing 30 by 5 gives 6 cookies per jar.\n\n**Answer:** There are 6 cookies in each jar.\n</think>\n\n**Solution:**\n\n1. **Determine the total number of cookies Lani ate.**\n   \n   Lani ate 5 cookies five times:\n   \\[\n   5 \\text{ cookies} \\times 5 \\text{ times} = 25 \\text{ cookies}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the number of cookies Lani has left after eating.**\n   \n   She baked a total of 55 cookies and ate 25:\n   \\[\n   55 \\text{ cookies} - 25 \\text{ cookies} = 30 \\text{ cookies}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Find out how many cookies are in each jar.**\n   \n   She placed the remaining cookies equally into five jars:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{30 \\text{ cookies}}{5 \\text{ jars}} = 6 \\text{ cookies per jar}\n   \\]\n\n**Answer:** \\(\\boxed{6}\\) cookies were in each jar.", "pred_ans": "6", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Lani baked 55 cookies. She ate 5 five cookies and placed the rest equally into five jars. How many cookies were in each jar?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
