{"question": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: John decides to get a loan by mortgaging his home.  His house is worth $250,000.  He gets a loan worth 40% of that.  He uses 60% of that to pay off his debts.  How much money did he have leftover after paying debt?\n Solution:\n<think>\n", "gold_ans": "40,000", "rationale": "First, I need to determine the total amount of the loan John has taken out. Since his house is worth $250,000, 40% of that is the loan amount.\n\nNext, I'll calculate 40% of $250,000. This can be done by multiplying 0.40 by $250,000, which equals $100,000.\n\nNow, John uses 60% of the loan to pay off his debts. To find 60% of $100,000, I'll multiply 0.60 by $100,000, resulting in $60,000.\n\nFinally, to find out how much money John has leftover after paying off his debts, I'll subtract the $60,000 from the total loan amount of $100,000. This leaves him with $40,000 leftover.\n</think>\n\n**Problem:**\nJohn decides to get a loan by mortgaging his home. His house is worth \\$250,000. He gets a loan worth 40% of that. He uses 60% of that to pay off his debts. How much money did he have leftover after paying debt?\n\n**Solution:**\n\n1. **Calculate the Total Loan Amount:**\n   \n   John takes out 40% of his home's value as a loan.\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Loan Amount} = 40\\% \\times \\$250,\\!000 = 0.40 \\times \\$250,\\!000 = \\$100,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the Amount Used to Pay Off Debts:**\n   \n   John uses 60% of the loan to pay off his debts.\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Amount Used} = 60\\% \\times \\$100,\\!000 = 0.60 \\times \\$100,\\!000 = \\$60,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine the Money Leftover:**\n   \n   Subtract the amount used to pay off debts from the total loan amount.\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Money Leftover} = \\$100,\\!000 - \\$60,\\!000 = \\$40,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$40,\\!000}\n\\]", "pred_ans": "40,000", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: John decides to get a loan by mortgaging his home.  His house is worth $250,000.  He gets a loan worth 40% of that.  He uses 60% of that to pay off his debts.  How much money did he have leftover after paying debt?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
