{"question": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: It's April, and Mrs. Rylan has been busy on her farm planting different types of vegetables for the season. She has bought 20 packets of tomato seeds and 80 packets of celery seeds to plant. If a packet of tomato seeds costs $40 and a packet of celery seeds costs $30, how much money did she use to buy the seeds?\n Solution:\n<think>\n", "gold_ans": "3200", "rationale": "To determine how much money Mrs. Rylan spent on buying the seeds, I will follow these steps.\n\nFirst, I need to calculate the total cost of the tomato seeds. Since she bought 20 packets and each packet costs $40, I will multiply the number of packets by the cost per packet.\n\nNext, I will calculate the total cost of the celery seeds. Mrs. Rylan purchased 80 packets, and each packet of celery seeds costs $30. I will multiply the number of celery packets by the cost per packet to find the total expense for celery seeds.\n\nFinally, I will add the total costs of both tomato and celery seeds to find the overall amount of money spent on purchasing all the seeds.\n</think>\n\nSure, let's solve the problem step by step.\n\n**Problem:**\nMrs. Rylan bought 20 packets of tomato seeds and 80 packets of celery seeds. Each packet of tomato seeds costs \\$40, and each packet of celery seeds costs \\$30. We need to find out how much money she spent in total.\n\n**Solution:**\n\n1. **Calculate the cost of tomato seeds:**\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost of tomato seeds} = \\text{Number of tomato packets} \\times \\text{Cost per tomato packet}\n   \\]\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost of tomato seeds} = 20 \\times \\$40 = \\$800\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Calculate the cost of celery seeds:**\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost of celery seeds} = \\text{Number of celery packets} \\times \\text{Cost per celery packet}\n   \\]\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost of celery seeds} = 80 \\times \\$30 = \\$2,\\!400\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Calculate the