{"question": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: My kitchen floor has a total area of 200 SqFt. I want to install new square floor tiles that cost $12 each, and each tile side is 1ft in length. How much will it cost me to renovate my kitchen floor?\n Solution:\n<think>\n", "gold_ans": "2400", "rationale": "First, I need to determine the area of the kitchen floor that needs to be covered by the new tiles. The total area is 200 square feet.\n\nNext, I'll find the number of tiles required by dividing the total area by the area of one tile. Since each tile is 1 square foot, I'll divide 200 by 1, which gives me 200 tiles.\n\nThen, I'll calculate the total cost by multiplying the number of tiles by the cost per tile. With each tile costing $12 and 200 tiles needed, the total cost will be 200 multiplied by 12, resulting in $2,400.\n\nTherefore, the total cost to renovate the kitchen floor is $2,400.\n</think>\n\nSure, let's solve the problem step by step.\n\n**Problem:**  \nMy kitchen floor has a total area of **200 SqFt**. I want to install new square floor tiles that cost **\\$12** each, and each tile side is **1ft** in length. How much will it cost me to renovate my kitchen floor?\n\n---\n\n**Solution:**\n\n1. **Determine the total area of the kitchen floor:**\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Total Area} = 200 \\text{ SqFt}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Find the area of one tile:**\n   \n   Each tile is a square, so the area of one tile is:\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of one tile} = \\text{side length}^2 = 1 \\text{ft} \\times 1 \\text{ft} = 1 \\text{ SqFt}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the number of tiles needed:**\n   \n   To find out how many tiles are required to cover the entire kitchen floor, divide the total area by the area of one tile:\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of tiles} = \\frac{\\text{Total Area}}{\\text{Area of one tile}} = \\frac{200 \\text{ SqFt}}{1 \\text{ SqFt}} = 200 \\text{ tiles}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Compute the total cost:**\n   \n   Multiply the number of tiles by the cost per tile:\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Total Cost} = \\text{Number of tiles} \\times \\text{Cost per tile} = 200 \\times \\$12 = \\$2,\\!400\n   \\]\n\n---\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$2,\\!400}\n\\]", "pred_ans": "2,400", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: My kitchen floor has a total area of 200 SqFt. I want to install new square floor tiles that cost $12 each, and each tile side is 1ft in length. How much will it cost me to renovate my kitchen floor?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
