{"question": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Carson lives in an old house where the pipes will freeze if the temperature inside the house falls below 32 degrees. Every log of wood Carson burns heats the house up by 5 degrees. If it was 45 degrees during the day, and it's 33 degrees colder during the night compared to the day, how many logs does Carson need to burn to prevent the pipes from freezing?\n Solution:\n<think>\n", "gold_ans": "4", "rationale": "First, determine the temperature drop from the day to the night. It was 45 degrees during the day, and it's 33 degrees colder at night. To find the temperature at night, subtract 33 degrees from 45 degrees.\n\n45\u00b0 - 33\u00b0 = 12\u00b0\n\nNext, figure out how much the temperature needs to be raised to stay above freezing. The pipes will freeze if the temperature drops below 32 degrees, so the house needs to maintain a temperature of at least 32 degrees.\n\n32\u00b0 (minimum temperature to prevent freezing)\n\nNow, calculate how many degrees need to be added to the house each night to maintain the minimum temperature. Subtract the night temperature from the minimum temperature required.\n\n32\u00b0 - 12\u00b0 = 20\u00b0\n\nDetermine how many logs are needed to add 20 degrees to the house. Each log of wood burns and raises the temperature by 5 degrees.\n\n20\u00b0 / 5\u00b0 per log = 4 logs\n\nTherefore, Carson needs to burn 4 logs to prevent the pipes from freezing.\n</think>\n\n**Solution:**\n\nTo prevent the pipes from freezing, Carson needs to ensure the temperature inside the house stays above 32 degrees.\n\n1. **Determine the Night Temperature:**\n   \n   The temperature was 45 degrees during the day. It is 33 degrees colder at night.\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Night Temperature} = 45^\\circ - 33^\\circ = 12^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the Temperature Needed to Prevent Freezing:**\n   \n   The house must stay at or above **32 degrees** to prevent freezing.\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Required Temperature} = 32^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n3. **Find Out How Much Additional Heat is Needed:**\n   \n   Compare the night temperature to the required temperature.\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Additional Heat Needed} = 32^\\circ - 12^\\circ = 20^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n4. **Determine the Number of Logs Needed:**\n   \n   Each log burns and raises the temperature by **5 degrees**.\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of Logs} = \\frac{20^\\circ}{5^\\circ \\text{ per log}} = 4 \\text{ logs}\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{4}\n\\]", "pred_ans": "4", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Carson lives in an old house where the pipes will freeze if the temperature inside the house falls below 32 degrees. Every log of wood Carson burns heats the house up by 5 degrees. If it was 45 degrees during the day, and it's 33 degrees colder during the night compared to the day, how many logs does Carson need to burn to prevent the pipes from freezing?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
