{"question": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Tatiana is deciding how much of her weekend she wants to spend playing soccer. She has 7 hours on Saturday and 5 hours on Sunday. She is dividing her time between soccer, video games, and reading. If she reads for 3 hours and plays video games for 1/3 of the remaining time, what percentage of her weekend does she spend playing soccer?\n Solution:\n<think>\n", "gold_ans": "50", "rationale": "To determine the percentage of Tatiana's weekend dedicated to playing soccer, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total hours available over the weekend.**\n   - **Saturday:** 7 hours\n   - **Sunday:** 5 hours\n   - **Total:** 7 + 5 = 12 hours\n\n2. **Determine the time spent on activities other than soccer.**\n   - **Reading:** 3 hours\n   - **Video Games:** (1/3) of the remaining time after reading\n   - **Remaining time after reading:** 12 hours - 3 hours = 9 hours\n   - **Video Games:** (1/3) * 9 hours = 3 hours\n\n3. **Calculate the total time spent on non-soccer activities.**\n   - **Total non-soccer time:** 3 hours (reading) + 3 hours (video games) = 6 hours\n\n4. **Find out the time dedicated to soccer.**\n   - **Soccer time:** Total time - Non-soccer time = 12 hours - 6 hours = 6 hours\n\n5. **Compute the percentage of the weekend spent on soccer.**\n   - **Percentage:** (Soccer time / Total time) * 100% = (6 / 12) * 100% = 50%\n\n**Answer:** 50% of her weekend is spent playing soccer.\n</think>\n\nTo determine the percentage of Tatiana's weekend dedicated to playing soccer, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total hours available over the weekend.**\n   \n   - **Saturday:** 7 hours\n   - **Sunday:** 5 hours\n   - **Total:** \\( 7 + 5 = 12 \\) hours\n\n2. **Determine the time spent on activities other than soccer.**\n   \n   - **Reading:** 3 hours\n   - **Video Games:** \\( \\frac{1}{3} \\) of the remaining time after reading\n   - **Remaining time after reading:** \\( 12 - 3 = 9 \\) hours\n   - **Video Games:** \\( \\frac{1}{3} \\times 9 = 3 \\) hours\n\n3. **Calculate the total time spent on non-soccer activities.**\n   \n   - **Total non-soccer time:** \\( 3 \\) hours (reading) + \\( 3 \\) hours (video games) = \\( 6 \\) hours\n\n4. **Find out the time dedicated to soccer.**\n   \n   - **Soccer time:** Total time - Non-soccer time = \\( 12 - 6 = 6 \\) hours\n\n5. **Compute the percentage of the weekend spent on soccer.**\n   \n   - **Percentage:** \\( \\left( \\frac{6}{12} \\right) \\times 100\\% = 50\\% \\)\n\n**Answer:** \\(\\boxed{50\\%}\\) of her weekend is spent playing soccer.", "pred_ans": "50", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Tatiana is deciding how much of her weekend she wants to spend playing soccer. She has 7 hours on Saturday and 5 hours on Sunday. She is dividing her time between soccer, video games, and reading. If she reads for 3 hours and plays video games for 1/3 of the remaining time, what percentage of her weekend does she spend playing soccer?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
