an 4 times as many as Adelwolfe. Let \\( A \\) be the number of Pok\u00e9mon Adelwolfe has caught. Then, Stan's total can be expressed as \\( S = 4A - 13 \\).\n\nTogether, they have caught 339 Pok\u00e9mon. Therefore, the equation for the total is:\n\\[\n(S + 5) + S + A = 339\n\\]\nSubstituting \\( S = 4A - 13 \\) into the equation, we get:\n\\[\n(4A - 13 + 5) + (4A - 13) + A = 339\n\\]\nSimplifying the equation:\n\\[\n4A - 13 + 5 + 4A - 13 + A = 339\n\\]\n\\[\n9A - 21 = 339\n\\]\nSolving for \\( A \\):\n\\[\n9A = 360\n\\]\n\\[\nA = 40\n\\]\nNow, substituting \\( A = 40 \\) back into the equation for \\( S \\):\n\\[\nS = 4 \\times 40 - 13\n\\]\n\\[\nS = 160 - 13\n\\]\n\\[\nS = 147\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of Pok\u00e9mon Stan has caught is \\(\\boxed{147}\\).", "pred_ans": "147", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Alex, Stan, and Adelwolfe are trying to catch them all, Pokemon that is.  Together they have caught 339 Pokemon.  Alex has caught 5 more than Stan, and Stan has caught 13 less than 4 times as many as Adelwolfe has caught. How many Pokemon has Stan caught?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
{"question": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: John decides to take up an odd hobby of speed talking.  His normally speaking speed is 150 WPM.  After training his speed is 2.5 times faster than his starting speed.  How long would it take him to speak 10 pages if each page has 450 words per page?\n Solution:\n<think>\n", "gold_ans": "12", "rationale": "To determine how long it will take John to speak 10 pages, we'll follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the new speaking speed after training:**\n   - Original speed = 150 words per minute (WPM)\n   - New speed = 2.5 times original speed\n   - New speed = 150 * 2.5 = 375 WPM\n\n2. **Find out how many words John can speak in one minute:**\n   - He speaks 375 words each minute.\n\n3. **Calculate the total number of words in 10 pages:**\n   - Words per page = 450\n   - Total words for 10 pages = 450 * 10 = 4500 words\n\n4. **Determine the time required to speak 4500 words at 375 WPM:**\n   - Time = Total words / Speaking speed\n   - Time = 4500 / 375 = 12 minutes\n</think>\n\nLet's solve the problem step by step.\n\n**Given:**\n- John's **original speaking speed** is **150 WPM** (words per minute).\n- After training, his speaking speed becomes **2.5 times** his original speed.\n- Each **page** has **450 words**.\n- John wants to speak **10 pages**.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate John's new speaking speed after training.**\n\n\\[\n\\text{New speed} = 2.5 \\times \\text{Original speed} = 2.5 \\times 150 = 375 \\text{ WPM}\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Determine the total number of words in 10 pages.**\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total words} = \\text{Words per page} \\times \\text{Number of pages} = 450 \\times 10 = 4500 \\text{ words}\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the time required to speak 4500 words at 375 WPM.**\n\n\\[\n\\text{Time} = \\frac{\\text{Total words}}{\\text{Speaking speed}} = \\frac{4500}{375} = 12 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{12 \\text{ minutes}}\n\\]", "pred_ans": "12", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: John decides to take up an odd hobby of speed talking.  His normally speaking speed is 150 WPM.  After training his speed is 2.5 times faster than his starting speed.  How long would it take him to speak 10 pages if each page has 450 words per page?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
