hese buttons have two holes each, and the remaining buttons have four holes each. We need to find the total number of holes in all the buttons.\n\n1. Calculate the number of buttons with four holes:\n   \\[\n   21 - 7 = 14\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate the number of holes in the buttons with two holes:\n   \\[\n   7 \\times 2 = 14\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate the number of holes in the buttons with four holes:\n   \\[\n   14 \\times 4 = 56\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the number of holes from both groups to find the total number of holes:\n   \\[\n   14 + 56 = 70\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total number of holes in all the buttons in the bag is \\(\\boxed{70}\\).", "pred_ans": "70", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: A bag of buttons had 21 buttons in it. Seven buttons had two holes and the rest had four holes. How many holes were in all the buttons in the bag?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
