{"question": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Audrey has to take two math tests to pass 6th grade. She must correctly answer 70% of the total questions to move on to the 7th grade. The first test has 70 questions and she gets 60% of them correct. The second test has 40 questions. How many questions does she need to get right on the second test to move onto the 7th grade?\n Solution:\n<think>\n", "gold_ans": "35", "rationale": "To determine how many questions Audrey needs to get right on the second test, I'll start by calculating the total number of questions she needs to answer correctly to pass both tests. Since she needs to answer 70% of the total questions correctly, I'll first find 70% of the combined number of questions from both tests.\n\nNext, I'll calculate the number of questions Audrey got right on the first test. She answered 60% of the 70 questions correctly. I'll compute 60% of 70 to find this out.\n\nAfter that, I'll determine how many questions she needs to get right on the second test to reach the total required correct answers. I'll subtract the number of correct answers from the first test from the total required to find the necessary number of correct answers on the second test.\n\nFinally, I'll verify that this number is a whole number since you can't answer a fraction of a question correctly. If it's not a whole number, I'll round up to the next whole number to ensure Audrey meets the passing criteria.\n\nBy following these steps, I'll find the exact number of questions Audrey needs to get right on the second test to move on to the 7th grade.\n</think>\n\n**Solution:**\n\nLet's break down the problem step by step to determine how many questions Audrey needs to get right on the second test.\n\n1. **Calculate the total number of questions Audrey needs to answer correctly to pass both tests:**\n\n   Audrey needs to answer **70%** of the total questions correctly to pass.\n\n   - **First te