{"question": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Pierre, Paul, and Jacques bought 12 kg of apples. Peter wants a quarter of that and Paul wants 1/3 of that. How many kilograms will James have left?\n Solution:\n<think>\n", "gold_ans": "5", "rationale": "First, I need to determine the total amount of apples that Pierre, Paul, and Jacques have together. They bought 12 kilograms of apples.\n\nNext, I'll figure out how much Peter wants. Peter wants a quarter of the total apples, so I'll calculate 1/4 of 12 kilograms.\n\nThen, Paul wants one-third of the apples. I'll compute 1/3 of 12 kilograms.\n\nAfter that, I'll add the amounts that Peter and Paul want together to find out how much they're taking from the total.\n\nFinally, I'll subtract the total taken by Peter and Paul from the original 12 kilograms to find out how many kilograms James will have left.\n</think>\n\nSure, let's break down the problem step by step.\n\n**Problem:**\nPierre, Paul, and Jacques bought 12 kg of apples. Peter wants a quarter of that and Paul wants 1/3 of that. How many kilograms will James have left?\n\n**Solution:**\n\n1. **Total Apples Purchased:**\n   \n   Pierre, Paul, and Jacques together bought:\n   \\[\n   12 \\text{ kg}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Amount Peter Wants:**\n   \n   Peter wants a quarter of the total apples:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{4} \\times 12 \\text{ kg} = 3 \\text{ kg}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Amount Paul Wants:**\n   \n   Paul wants one-third of the total apples:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{3} \\times 12 \\text{ kg} = 4 \\text{ kg}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Total Apples Taken by Peter and Paul:**\n   \n   Adding the amounts Peter and Paul want together:\n   \\[\n   3 \\text{ kg} + 4 \\text{ kg} = 7 \\text{ kg}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Apples Remaining for James:**\n   \n   Subtract the total taken by Peter and Paul from the original 12 kg:\n   \\[\n   12 \\text{ kg} - 7 \\text{ kg} = 5 \\text{ kg}\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{5}\n\\]", "pred_an