e denote the number of marbles Mazie gave to Dallas as \\( D \\) and the number she gave to Darla as \\( R \\). The total number of marbles is given by:\n\\[ D + R = 52 \\]\n\nAfter dropping 4 marbles, Dallas has:\n\\[ D - 4 = 21 \\]\n\nSolving for \\( D \\):\n\\[ D = 21 + 4 \\]\n\\[ D = 25 \\]\n\nNow, we find the number of marbles Darla received:\n\\[ R = 52 - D \\]\n\\[ R = 52 - 25 \\]\n\\[ R = 27 \\]\n\nThus, Mazie gave \\boxed{27} marbles to Darla.", "pred_ans": "27", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Mazie has 52 marbles and gives them to twins, Dallas and Darla.  If Dallas has a total of 21 marbles after dropping 4 of them in the playground, how many did Mazie give to Darla?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
