 case, the problem is giving a relationship between their ages in the future, so I think the way I approached it is correct.\n\nJust to recap:\n\n- Jame's current age: 22\n- In 8 years, Jame's age: 30\n- Cousin's age in 8 years: 5 years younger than twice Jame's age then, which is 55\n- Therefore, cousin's current age: 55 - 8 = 47\n- Difference in ages: 47 - 22 = 25\n\nSo, the age difference is 25 years.\n\nI think that makes sense. Let me consider an alternative approach to verify.\n\nAnother way to think about it is to set up equations.\n\nLet me denote:\nJame's current age = J\nCousin's current age = C\n\nFrom the first statement: J = 27 - 5 = 22\n\nFrom the second statement: In 8 years, cousin's age = 5 years younger than twice Jame's age in 8 years.\n\nSo, in 8 years:\nJame's age = J + 8 = 22 + 8 = 30\nCousin's age = C + 8\n\nAccording to the problem:\nC + 8 = 2*(J + 8) - 5\n\nPlugging in J = 22:\nC + 8 = 2*(22 + 8) - 5\nC + 8 = 2*30 - 5\nC + 8 = 60 - 5\nC + 8 = 55\nC = 55 - 8\nC = 47\n\nSo, cousin's current age is 47. The age difference is C - J = 47 - 22 = 25 years.\n\nYes, same result. That's reassuring.\n\nJust to make sure, let's think about it in terms of age differences. The age difference between the cousin and Jame should remain constant over time. So, in 8 years, the cousin will be 55 and Jame will be 30. The difference then is 55 - 30 = 25 years. So, the age difference is indeed 25 years now, which means the cousin is 25 years older than Jame. So, yes, that's consistent.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 25 years.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe age difference between Jame and his cousin is \\boxed{25} years.\n</think>\n\nJame's current age is calculated as follows:\n- Jame will turn 27 in 5 years, so his current age is \\(27 - 5 = 22\\) years old.\n\nIn 8 years, Jame's age will be:\n- \\(22 + 8 = 30\\) years old.\n\nAt that time, his cousin will be 5 years younger than twice Jame's age:\n- Twice Jame's age in 8 years is \\(2 \\times 30 = 60\\).\n- Therefore, the cousin's age in 8 years will be \\(60 - 5 = 55\\) years old.\n\nThe cousin's current age is:\n- \\(55 - 8 = 47\\) years old.\n\nThe difference in their ages is:\n- \\(47 - 22 = 25\\) years.\n\nThus, the age difference between Jame and his cousin is \\(\\boxed{25}\\) years.", "pred_ans": "25", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Jame will turn 27 in 5 years.  In 8 years his cousin will be 5 years younger than twice his age.  How many years separate the age of the two now?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
