{"question": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: A company produces chocolate in bars. In one day, it can produce 5000 bars. The company sells all the produced bars for $2 per bar. How much money will the company receive for selling produced chocolate bars during two weeks?\n Solution:\n<think>\n", "gold_ans": "140000", "rationale": "To solve this problem, I'll follow these steps:\n\n1. **Determine the number of days in two weeks.**\n   - A week has 7 days, so two weeks equal 14 days.\n\n2. **Calculate the number of chocolate bars produced per day.**\n   - The company produces 5000 bars each day.\n\n3. **Find the total number of chocolate bars produced over two weeks.**\n   - Multiply the daily production by the number of days:\n   5000 bars/day * 14 days = 70,000 bars.\n\n4. **Calculate the revenue from selling all the chocolate bars.**\n   - Each bar is sold for $2, so multiply the total number of bars by the selling price:\n   70,000 bars * $2/bar = $140,000.\n\nTherefore, the company will receive \\boxed{\\$140000} for selling the produced chocolate bars during two weeks.\n</think>\n\nTo determine how much money the company will receive for selling the chocolate bars during two weeks, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Determine the number of days in two weeks:**\n   \\[\n   2 \\text{ weeks} \\times 7 \\text{ days/week} = 14 \\text{ days}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the number of chocolate bars produced each day:**\n   \\[\n   5000 \\text{ bars/day}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Find the total number of chocolate bars produced over two weeks:**\n   \\[\n   5000 \\text{ bars/day} \\times 14 \\text{ days} = 70,\\!000 \\text{ bars}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the revenue from selling all the chocolate bars:**\n   \\[\n   70,\\!000 \\text{ bars} \\times \\$2/\\text{bar} = \\$140,\\!000\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the company will receive \\boxed{\\$140000} for selling the produced chocolate bars during two weeks.", "pred_ans": "140000", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: A company produces chocolate in bars. In one day, it can produce 5000 bars. The company sells all the produced bars for $2 per bar. How much money will the company receive for selling produced chocolate bars during two weeks?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
