{"question": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Christina is planning a birthday party and needs .75 gift bags per invited guest, because 1/4 of attendees don't show up. She invited 16 friends. Gift bags are $2 each. How much will she spend?\n Solution:\n<think>\n", "gold_ans": "24", "rationale": "First, I need to determine how many gift bags Christina will need. Since she invited 16 friends and 1/4 of them might not show up, I should calculate 3/4 of 16 to find the expected number of attendees.\n\nNext, I'll calculate the total cost by multiplying the number of gift bags by the cost per bag. Christina is spending $2 on each gift bag.\n\nFinally, I'll add up all the costs to find out how much she will spend in total.\n</think>\n\nLet's solve the problem step by step.\n\n**Problem:**\nChristina is planning a birthday party and needs **0.75 gift bags per invited guest**, because \\( \\frac{1}{4} \\) of attendees don't show up. She invited **16 friends**. Gift bags are **\\$2 each**. How much will she spend?\n\n---\n\n**Solution:**\n\n1. **Calculate the number of gift bags needed:**\n\n   Since \\( \\frac{1}{4} \\) of the invited guests might not show up, Christina should prepare for \\( \\frac{3}{4} \\) of the invited guests.\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of guests to prepare for} = \\frac{3}{4} \\times 16 = 12 \\text{ gift bags}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the total cost of gift bags:**\n\n   Each gift bag costs \\$2.\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total cost} = 12 \\times 2 = \\$24\n   \\]\n\n---\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\nChristina will spend \\(\\boxed{24}\\) dollars.", "pred_ans": "24", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Christina is planning a birthday party and needs .75 gift bags per invited guest, because 1/4 of attendees don't show up. She invited 16 friends. Gift bags are $2 each. How much will she spend?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
