an a half-gallon jar, and a gallon jar costs $5. To find the cost of a half-gallon jar, we set up the equation:\n\n\\[ x + 2 = 5 \\]\n\nSolving for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[ x = 5 - 2 \\]\n\\[ x = 3 \\]\n\nThus, a half-gallon jar costs $3. \n\nNext, we calculate the cost for 10-gallon jars and 16 half-gallon jars:\n\n- The cost for 10-gallon jars is:\n  \\[ 10 \\times 5 = 50 \\]\n\n- The cost for 16 half-gallon jars is:\n  \\[ 16 \\times 3 = 48 \\]\n\nAdding these together gives the total cost:\n\n\\[ 50 + 48 = 98 \\]\n\nTherefore, the total amount of money Cecelia spent is \\boxed{98} dollars.", "pred_ans": "98", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Cecelia went to the milk store and found out that a gallon jar costs $2 more than a half-gallon jar. If a gallon jar costs $5, calculate the total amount of money she spent on 10-gallon jars and 16 half-gallon jars.\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
