\[ L = \\frac{120,000}{4} = 30,000 \\]\n\nThe cost of the house is \\( 3L \\):\n\n\\[ 3L = 3 \\times 30,000 = 90,000 \\]\n\nThus, the house cost \\boxed{90000} dollars.", "pred_ans": "90000", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: A house and a lot cost $120,000. If the house cost three times as much as the lot, how much did the house cost?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
