ivered from Monday to Wednesday.\n\nWait, just to make sure I didn't misinterpret the problem. Let me go back.\n\n\"425 letters on Monday. Tuesday: 17 more than one-fifth as Monday. So, that's one-fifth of 425 which is 85, plus 17 is 102. Wednesday: 5 more than twice as Tuesday. So, twice 102 is 204, plus 5 is 209. Then total is 425 + 102 + 209. Hmm, 425 + 102 is 527, plus 209 is 736. Yeah, that's consistent.\n\nI don't see any mistakes in my reasoning. So, I think 736 is the correct answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe total number of letters delivered Monday to Wednesday is \\boxed{736}.\n</think>\n\nOn Monday, the post office delivered 425 letters.\n\nOn Tuesday, they delivered 17 more than one-fifth as many as Monday. One-fifth of 425 is calculated as follows:\n\\[\n\\frac{425}{5} = 85\n\\]\nAdding 17 to this amount:\n\\[\n85 + 17 = 102\n\\]\nSo, they delivered 102 letters on Tuesday.\n\nOn Wednesday, they delivered 5 more than twice as many as they delivered on Tuesday. Twice the number of letters delivered on Tuesday is:\n\\[\n2 \\times 102 = 204\n\\]\nAdding 5 to this amount:\n\\[\n204 + 5 = 209\n\\]\nSo, they delivered 209 letters on Wednesday.\n\nTo find the total number of letters delivered from Monday to Wednesday, we sum the letters delivered each day:\n\\[\n425 + 102 + 209 = 736\n\\]\n\nThus, the total number of letters delivered Monday to Wednesday is \\boxed{736}.", "pred_ans": "736", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: On Monday the post office delivered 425 letters. On Tuesday they delivered 17 more than one-fifth as many as Monday. On Wednesday they delivered 5 more than twice as many as they delivered on Tuesday. How many letters did the post office deliver Monday - Wednesday?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
