itrus Zest = z\n- Fragrance = z\n- Oil = 2s = 4z\n\nSo, all the quantities can be expressed in terms of 'z', which is the amount of citrus zest.\n\nNow, let's calculate the total weight of all the ingredients:\n\n1. Salt: 2z ounces\n2. Sugar: 2z ounces\n3. Citrus Zest: z ounces\n4. Fragrance: z ounces\n5. Oil: 4z ounces\n\nAdding all these together: 2z + 2z + z + z + 4z = 10 ounces (since the jar is 10 ounces).\n\nLet me compute that total:\n\n2z (salt) + 2z (sugar) + z (zest) + z (fragrance) + 4z (oil) = 10 ounces\n\nAdding like terms:\n\n2z + 2z is 4z\n4z + z is 5z\n5z + z is 6z\n6z + 4z is 10z\n\nSo, 10z = 10 ounces.\n\nTherefore, z = 1 ounce.\n\nNow, since oil is 4z, and z is 1 ounce, then oil is 4 times 1 ounce, which is 4 ounces.\n\nWait, let me double-check. If z is 1, then:\n\n- Salt = 2z = 2 ounces\n- Sugar = 2 ounces\n- Citrus Zest = 1 ounce\n- Fragrance = 1 ounce\n- Oil = 4 ounces\n\nAdding those up: 2 + 2 + 1 + 1 + 4 = 10 ounces. Yes, that adds up correctly.\n\nSo, the amount of oil she uses is 4 ounces.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe number of ounces of oil Tanya uses is \\boxed{4}.\n</think>\n\nLet's break down the problem step by step:\n\n1. Tanya makes a salt scrub using salt, oil, fragrance, citrus zest, and sugar, each time filling a 10-ounce jar.\n2. She uses the same amount of citrus zest as fragrance and the same amount of salt as sugar.\n3. She uses twice as much oil as salt and twice as much salt as zest.\n\nLet's denote:\n- The amount of salt as \\( s \\) ounces.\n- The amount of sugar as \\( s \\) ounces (since she uses the same amount of salt as sugar).\n- The amount of citrus zest as \\( z \\) ounces.\n- The amount of fragrance as \\( z \\) ounces (since she uses the same amount of citrus zest as fragrance).\n- The amount of oil as \\( 2s \\) ounces (since she uses twice as much oil as salt).\n\nAdditionally, since she uses twice as much salt as zest:\n- Salt \\( s = 2z \\).\n\nExpressing all quantities in terms of \\( z \\):\n- Salt \\( s = 2z \\)\n- Sugar \\( = 2z \\)\n- Citrus Zest \\( = z \\)\n- Fragrance \\( = z \\)\n- Oil \\( = 2s = 2(2z) = 4z \\)\n\nThe total weight of all ingredients is 10 ounces:\n- Salt: \\(2z\\)\n- Sugar: \\(2z\\)\n- Citrus Zest: \\(z\\)\n- Fragrance: \\(z\\)\n- Oil: \\(4z\\)\n\nAdding these together:\n\\[2z + 2z + z + z + 4z = 10\\]\n\\[10z = 10\\]\n\\[z = 1\\]\n\nThus, the amount of oil is:\n\\[4z = 4 \\times 1 = 4\\]\n\nThe number of ounces of oil Tanya uses is \\(\\boxed{4}\\).", "pred_ans": "4", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Tanya makes a salt scrub from salt, oil, fragrance, citrus zest, and sugar. She makes enough to fill a 10-ounce jar each time. She uses the same amount of citrus zest as fragrance and the same amount of salt as sugar. She uses twice as much oil as salt and twice as much salt as zest. How many ounces of oil does she use?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
