ac{8 \\text{ feet}}{2 \\text{ feet/hour}} = 4 \\text{ hours}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Total time to dig the well:**\n   \\[\n   Total \\ Time = Time_{\\text{soil}} + Time_{\\text{clay}} = 6 \\text{ hours} + 4 \\text{ hours} = 10 \\text{ hours}\n   \\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{10}\n\\]", "pred_ans": "10", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Bill is trying to dig a well in his backyard. He can dig 4 feet/hour through soil and half that fast through clay. If he has to dig through 24 feet of soil and 8 feet of clay, how long will it take him to dig the well?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
