{"question": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Six years ago, when Noah was half as old as Cera, the population of Chile was half what it is now. Currently, Cera is 46 years old. If the population of Chile six years ago was 3000 times the age of Noah, calculate the population of Chile now.\n Solution:\n<think>\n", "gold_ans": "120000", "rationale": "Okay, so I've got this math problem to solve, and I need to figure it out step by step. Let me read it again to make sure I understand all the details.\n\nThe problem says: Six years ago, when Noah was half as old as Cera, the population of Chile was half what it is now. Currently, Cera is 46 years old. If the population of Chile six years ago was 3000 times the age of Noah, calculate the population of Chile now.\n\nAlright, let's break this down. There are two main people involved: Noah and Cera. We're given some information about their ages six years ago and the population of Chile at that time. We need to find the current population of Chile.\n\nFirst, let's list out the information we have:\n\n1. Currently, Cera is 46 years old.\n2. Six years ago, Noah was half as old as Cera was at that time.\n3. Six years ago, the population of Chile was half of its current population.\n4. Six years ago, the population of Chile was 3000 times the age of Noah.\n\nSo, we need to figure out the current population of Chile. Let's denote variables for the unknowns.\n\nLet me define:\n\n- Let N = current population of Chile.\n- Let noah_current = Noah's current age.\n- Let cera_current = Cera's current age. We know this is 46.\n\nSo, cera_current = 46.\n\nSix years ago, Cera was (46 - 6) = 40 years old.\n\nAt that time, Noah was half as old as Cera was. So, Noah's age six years ago was half of 40.\n\nSo, noah_six_years_ago = (1/2) * 40 = 20.\n\nSo, six years ago, Noah was 20 years old.\n\nSo, Noah's current age is noah_current = noah_six_years_ago + 6 = 20 + 6 = 26.\n\nWait, hold on. Let me make sure I did that correctly.\n\nIf Noah was 20 six years ago, adding six years gives us his current age. So, 20 + 6 = 26. So, Noah is currently 26 years old.\n\nSo, now we know Cera is 46 and Noah is 26.\n\nNow, the problem also mentions the population of Chile. Let's denote the current population as P.\n\nSix years ago, the population was half of what it is now, so population_six_years_ago = (1/2) * P.\n\nAlso, it's given that six years ago, the population of Chile was 3000 times the age of Noah at that time. So, population_six_years_ago = 3000 * noah_six_years_ago.\n\nWe already have noah_six_years_ago = 20.\n\nSo, population_six_years_ago = 3000 * 20 = 60,000.\n\nBut we also have that population_six_years_ago = (1/2) * P.\n\nSo, 60,000 = (1/2) * P.\n\nTherefore, to find P, we can solve for it:\n\nP = 60,000 * 2 = 120,000.\n\nSo, the current population of Chile is 120,000.\n\nWait, let me double-check to make sure I haven't missed anything.\n\nSo, six years ago, Noah was 20, which is half of Cera's age at that time (40). The population was half of now, which is 60,000. But then, 60,000 was also 3000 times Noah's age then, so 3000*20=60,000.\n\nYes, that seems consistent.\n\nTherefore, the current population is double that, so 120,000.\n\nI think that makes sense. Let me go through it again to ensure I haven't missed any steps.\n\n1. Cera is currently 46, so six years ago, she was 40.\n2. At that time, Noah was half as old as Cera, so Noah was 20.\n3. Six years ago, the population of Chile was half of the current population, so (1/2)*P.\n4. Also, six years ago, the population was 3000 times Noah's age, which is 3000*20=60,000.\n5. So, (1/2)*P = 60,000, so P=120,000.\n\nYes, that seems correct.\n\nI think that's all the steps needed. I don't see any errors in the calculations or the logic.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe population of Chile now is \\boxed{120000}.\n</think>\n\nGiven the problem, we need to calculate the current population of Chile. Let's break down the information step by step:\n\n1. Currently, Cera is 46 years old. Therefore, six years ago, Cera was \\(46 - 6 = 40\\) years old.\n2. Six years ago, Noah was half as old as Cera. Thus, Noah's age six years ago was \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times 40 = 20\\) years.\n3. Let \\(P\\) be the current population of Chile. Six years ago, the population of Chile was half of the current population, which is \\(\\frac{1}{2}P\\).\n4. It is also given that six years ago, the population of Chile was 3000 times the age of Noah. Therefore, six years ago, the population was \\(3000 \\times 20 = 60000\\).\n\nSince six years ago, the population of Chile was both \\(\\frac{1}{2}P\\) and 60000, we can set up the equation:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{2}P = 60000\n\\]\nSolving for \\(P\\):\n\\[\nP = 60000 \\times 2 = 120000\n\\]\n\nThus, the current population of Chile is \\(\\boxed{120000}\\).", "pred_ans": "120000", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Six years ago, when Noah was half as old as Cera, the population of Chile was half what it is now. Currently, Cera is 46 years old. If the population of Chile six years ago was 3000 times the age of Noah, calculate the population of Chile now.\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
