med.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe number of flowers that have bloomed in Arianna's garden is \\boxed{160}.\n</think>\n\nArianna plants a garden with 10 rows of flowers, each row containing 20 flowers. To find the total number of flowers, we multiply the number of rows by the number of flowers per row:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total flowers} = 10 \\times 20 = 200\n\\]\n\nCurrently, only \\(\\frac{4}{5}\\) of the planted flowers have bloomed. To find out how many flowers have bloomed, we calculate \\(\\frac{4}{5}\\) of the total number of flowers:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Bloomed flowers} = \\frac{4}{5} \\times 200\n\\]\n\nFirst, we convert the fraction to a decimal:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{4}{5} = 0.8\n\\]\n\nThen, we multiply the total number of flowers by this decimal:\n\n\\[\n0.8 \\times 200 = 160\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of flowers that have bloomed in Arianna's garden is \\(\\boxed{160}\\).", "pred_ans": "160", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Arianna plants a garden that has 10 rows of flowers with 20 flowers in each row. Currently, only 4/5 of the planted flowers have bloomed. How many flowers in Arianna's garden have bloomed?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
