{"question": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: John and DeSean bought a bag of marshmallows to make s'mores together. The bag has 35 marshmallows. Each S'more uses one marshmallow. If John makes 9 S'mores, DeSean makes 9 S'mores, and they dropped 3 marshmallows on the ground, how many S'mores can each kid have with the marshmallows left in the bag?\n Solution:\n<think>\n", "gold_ans": "7", "rationale": "John and DeSean have a bag with 35 marshmallows. They each make 9 s'mores, which uses 1 marshmallow each. So, together they use 9 + 9 = 18 marshmallows. After making the s'mores, they drop 3 marshmallows on the ground. That means they have 35 - 18 - 3 = 14 marshmallows left. Since each s'more requires 1 marshmallow, each kid can have 14 / 2 = 7 s'mores left.\n\nStep-by-Step Explanation:\n1. Total marshmallows: 35\n2. Marshmallows used by John: 9\n3. Marshmallows used by DeSean: 9\n4. Total marshmallows used: 9 + 9 = 18\n5. Marshmallows dropped: 3\n6. Marshmallows left: 35 - 18 - 3 = 14\n7. Number of marshmallows each can have: 14 \u00f7 2 = 7\n\nFinal Answer:\nEach kid can have \\boxed{7} s'mores with the marshmallows left in the bag.\n</think>\n\nJohn and DeSean have a bag with 35 marshmallows. They each make 9 s'mores, which uses 1 marshmallow each. So, together they use 9 + 9 = 18 marshmallows. After making the s'mores, they drop 3 marshmallows on the ground. That means they have 35 - 18 - 3 = 14 marshmallows left. Since each s'more requires 1 marshmallow, each kid can have 14 / 2 = 7 s'mores left.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Total marshmallows} & : 35 \\\\\n\\text{Marshmallows used by John} & : 9 \\\\\n\\text{Marshmallows used by DeSean} & : 9 \\\\\n\\text{Total marshmallows used} & : 9 + 9 = 18 \\\\\n\\text{Marshmallows dropped} & : 3 \\\\\n\\text{Marshmallows left} & : 35 - 18 - 3 = 14 \\\\\n\\text{Number of marshmallows each can have} & : \\frac{14}{2} = 7 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nEach kid can have \\boxed{7} s'mores with the marshmallows left in the bag.", "pred_ans": "7", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: John and DeSean bought a bag of marshmallows to make s'mores together. The bag has 35 marshmallows. Each S'more uses one marshmallow. If John makes 9 S'mores, DeSean makes 9 S'mores, and they dropped 3 marshmallows on the ground, how many S'mores can each kid have with the marshmallows left in the bag?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
