n- The normal cost is $120 per month.\n- A 60% increase on $120 is calculated as \\(120 \\times 0.6 = 72\\).\n- Therefore, the increased monthly cost is \\(120 + 72 = 192\\).\n\nNext, we calculate the annual cost by multiplying the monthly cost by 12:\n- The monthly cost is $192.\n- The annual cost is \\(192 \\times 12 = 2304\\).\n\nThus, James pays \\boxed{2304} dollars a year. \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2304}\n\\]", "pred_ans": "2304", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: James has to buy insurance.  Since he had an accident it was 60% more than normal.  The normal cost is $120 a month.  How much does he pay a year?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
