eeded** = 54 \u00f7 8 = 6.75\n\n3. **Since Mr. Jackson can only buy whole packs** and he expects to have some extra glue sticks left over:\n   \n   - He needs to buy **7 packs** to have enough glue sticks for all students.\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\\boxed{7}", "pred_ans": "7", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Mr. Jackson\u2019s fourth-grade class has 27 students. He wants to give each student 2 glue sticks. The glue sticks come in packs of 8. How many packs will Mr. Jackson need to buy so every student can have 2 glue sticks, assuming he can only buy whole packs and he expects to have some extra glue sticks left over?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
