 ounces.\n</think>\n\nRory makes a cake that weighs 20 ounces. She cuts it into 8 equal pieces, so each piece weighs \\( \\frac{20}{8} = 2.5 \\) ounces. Rory and her mom each have one piece, so together they have \\( 2 \\times 2.5 = 5 \\) ounces. The remaining cake weighs \\( 20 - 5 = 15 \\) ounces.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{15}\n\\]", "pred_ans": "15", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Rory makes a cake that weighs 20 ounces. She cuts into 8 pieces. Rory and her mom each have a piece. How much does the remaining cake weigh?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
