 previous one.\n\nJust to recap:\n\n- Tobias: 20 seconds.\n- Chikote: 2 * 20 = 40 seconds.\n- Igneous: 20 + 40 = 60 seconds.\n- Total: 20 + 40 + 60 = 120 seconds = 2 minutes.\n\nYep, that seems right.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe combined length of time of the three wolves' howls is \\boxed{2} minutes.\n</think>\n\nTobias howls for 20 seconds. Chikote howls for twice as long as Tobias, so Chikote's howl time is \\(2 \\times 20 = 40\\) seconds. Igneous howls for as long as the other two wolves combined, so Igneous's howl time is \\(20 + 40 = 60\\) seconds. \n\nAdding the howl times together:\n\n\\[\n20 \\text{ seconds (Tobias)} + 40 \\text{ seconds (Chikote)} + 60 \\text{ seconds (Igneous)} = 120 \\text{ seconds}\n\\]\n\nConverting the total time from seconds to minutes:\n\n\\[\n120 \\text{ seconds} \\div 60 = 2 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nThe combined length of time of the three wolves' howls is \\(\\boxed{2}\\) minutes.", "pred_ans": "2", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Tobias, Chikote, and Igneous are the three little wolves who live in the forest and howl at the moon every night. When Tobias howls, each howl lasts for a total of 20 seconds.  Chikote howls for twice as long as Tobias.  And Igneous howls for as long as the other two wolves combined.  What is the combined length of time, in minutes, of the three wolves' howls?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
{"question": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Gomer ate 5 less than 23 scoops of mashed potatoes.  If it takes 3 less than 6 potatoes to make 1 less than 3 scoops of mashed potatoes, how many potatoes did Gomer eat?\n Solution:\n<think>\n", "gold_ans": "27", "rationale": "Alright, so I need to solve this math problem about Gomer eating mashed potatoes. Let me try to break it down step by step. \n\nFirst, the problem says: \"Gomer ate 5 less than 23 scoops of mashed potatoes.\" Okay, so that part seems straightforward. If I have 23 scoops and Gomer ate 5 less than that, I think I can write that as 23 minus 5. Let me calculate that:\n\n23 - 5 = 18\n\nSo, Gomer ate 18 scoops of mashed potatoes. Wait, no, hold on. Let me make sure I'm interpreting that correctly. \"5 less than 23\" means I subtract 5 from 23, right? Yeah, so 23 minus 5 is indeed 18. So, Gomer ate 18 scoops. Got that.\n\nBut then the next part says: \"If it takes 3 less than 6 potatoes to make 1 less than 3 scoops of mashed potatoes, how many potatoes did Gomer eat?\" Hmm, okay, so now I need to figure out how many potatoes Gomer ate based on this relationship.\n\nLet me parse this sentence carefully. It says, \"it takes 3 less than 6 potatoes to make 1 less than 3 scoops of mashed potatoes.\" So, breaking that down:\n\n1. \"3 less than 6 potatoes\" - that would be 6 minus 3, which is 3 potatoes.\n2. \"1 less than 3 scoops of mashed potatoes\" - that would be 3 minus 1, which is 2 scoops.\n\nSo, putting that together: it takes 3 potatoes to make 2 scoops of mashed potatoes. Hmm, so 3 potatoes make 2 scoops. I need to find out how many potatoes Gomer ate, but Gomer ate 18 scoops, right? So, if 3 potatoes make 2 scoops, how many potatoes would it take to make 18 scoops?\n\nWait, let me make sure I'm translating that correctly. The problem is a bit of a chain: \"3 less than 6 potatoes to make 1 less than 3 scoops.\" So, 3 less than 6 is 3 potatoes,