{"question": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: John plans to save money from working.  He gets paid $2 per hour and works 5 hours a day for 4 days a week.  If he wants to save $80 how many weeks will it take him?\n Solution:\n<think>\n", "gold_ans": "2", "rationale": "To determine how many weeks John needs to work to save $80, I'll start by calculating his daily earnings.\n\nHe earns $2 per hour and works 5 hours each day. So, his daily income is 2 multiplied by 5, which equals $10.\n\nNext, I'll calculate his weekly savings by multiplying his daily earnings by the number of days he works in a week. That's 10 multiplied by 4, resulting in $40 per week.\n\nFinally, to find out how many weeks he needs to save $80, I'll divide the total amount he wants to save by his weekly savings. So, 80 divided by 40 equals 2 weeks.\n</think>\n\n**Solution:**\n\nLet's break down John's savings step by step.\n\n1. **Calculate John's daily earnings:**\n   \n   John earns \\$2 per hour and works for 5 hours each day.\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Daily Earnings} = \\$2 \\text{ per hour} \\times 5 \\text{ hours/day} = \\$10 \\text{ per day}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate John's weekly savings:**\n   \n   He works 4 days each week.\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Weekly Earnings} = \\$10 \\text{ per day} \\times 4 \\text{ days/week} = \\$40 \\text{ per week}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine how many weeks are needed to save \\$80:**\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of Weeks} = \\frac{\\$80 \\text{ desired savings}}{\\$40 \\text{ per week}} = 2 \\text{ weeks}\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]", "pred_ans": "2", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: John plans to save money from working.  He gets paid $2 per hour and works 5 hours a day for 4 days a week.  If he wants to save $80 how many weeks will it take him?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
