e fee to rent the theater is $125 for a party of 20, plus $6 for each additional guest. Kayla invited her 25 classmates, 7 girls in her dance class, and 13 family members. \n\nFirst, we calculate the total number of people invited:\n\\[ 25 \\text{ classmates} + 7 \\text{ dance classmates} + 13 \\text{ family members} = 45 \\text{ people} \\]\n\nHowever, 4 people said they could not come, so the number of people attending the party is:\n\\[ 45 - 4 = 41 \\text{ people} \\]\n\nThe base fee is $125 for 20 people. The number of additional guests is:\n\\[ 41 - 20 = 21 \\text{ additional guests} \\]\n\nThe cost for the additional guests is:\n\\[ 21 \\times 6 = 126 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nTherefore, the total cost of the party is:\n\\[ 125 + 126 = 251 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{251}\n\\]", "pred_ans": "251", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Kayla is having her birthday party at a movie theater. The fee to rent the theater is $125 for a party of 20, plus $6 for each additional guest. Kayla invited her 25 classmates and the 7 girls in her dance class, as well as 13 family members. Only 4 people said they could not come. How much will the party cost?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
