onday: 8\n\nTuesday and Wednesday: 6 each, so 12 total.\n\nThursday to Sunday: 7 each, so 28 total.\n\n8 + 12 = 20; 20 + 28 = 48.\n\nYes, same result.\n\nSo, 48 hours in total.\n\nWait, 48 hours? That seems like a lot. Let me just make sure that I interpreted the problem correctly.\n\nThe problem says: Sadie slept 8 hours on Monday. For the next two days, she slept 2 hours less, each, because she had to complete some assignments. If the rest of the week she slept 1 hour more than those two days, how many hours did she sleep in total throughout the week?\n\nSo, yeah, \"for the next two days, she slept 2 hours less, each,\" so each of those days is 2 hours less than Monday. So, 8 - 2 = 6 each on Tuesday and Wednesday.\n\nThen, the rest of the week, which is four days, she slept 1 hour more than those two days. So, \"those two days\" refers to Tuesday and Wednesday, which were 6 hours each. So, 6 + 1 = 7 hours each day for the rest of the week.\n\nSo, that would be Thursday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday, each 7 hours.\n\nSo, that adds up to: 8 + 6 + 6 + 7 + 7 + 7 + 7.\n\nLet me do that addition in a different way.\n\n8 + 6 is 14.\n\n14 + 6 is 20.\n\n20 + 7 is 27.\n\n27 + 7 is 34.\n\n34 + 7 is 41.\n\n41 + 7 is 48.\n\nYes, so 48 hours total.\n\nBut, 48 hours is 2 days worth of sleep. That's a lot. Is that reasonable? Maybe Sadie is a very heavy sleeper, or perhaps she is working a lot.\n\nBut, in any case, the problem is about calculating the total, not about whether it's a lot or not.\n\nSo, I think I did it correctly.\n\nSo, the total hours she slept throughout the week: 48 hours.\n\n**Final Answer**\nSadie slept a total of \\boxed{48} hours throughout the week.\n</think>\n\nSadie slept 8 hours on Monday. For the next two days, Tuesday and Wednesday, she slept 2 hours less each day, which means 6 hours each day. For the rest of the week (Thursday, Friday, Saturday, and Sunday), she slept 1 hour more than those two days, which means 7 hours each day.\n\nCalculating the tota