{"question": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Travis had 61 apps on his tablet. He deleted 9 apps he didn't use anymore and downloaded 18 more. How many apps are on his tablet now?\n Solution:\n<think>\n", "gold_ans": "70", "rationale": "Travis started with 61 apps on his tablet. He deleted 9 apps that he no longer used. After deleting, the number of remaining apps is calculated by subtracting the deleted apps from the initial total. That gives us 61 minus 9, which equals 52 apps.\n\nThen, Travis downloaded 18 more apps. To find the total number of apps on his tablet now, we add the downloaded apps to the remaining apps. So, we add 18 to 52, resulting in 70 apps.\n\nTherefore, Travis has 70 apps on his tablet now.\n</think>\n\nSure, let's break down the problem step by step.\n\n**Problem:**\nTravis had 61 apps on his tablet. He deleted 9 apps he didn't use anymore and downloaded 18 more. How many apps are on his tablet now?\n\n---\n\n**Solution:**\n\n1. **Initial Number of Apps:**\n   - Travis started with **61 apps** on his tablet.\n\n2. **Delete Unused Apps:**\n   - He deleted **9 apps** that he no longer used.\n   - To find out how many apps are left after deleting:\n     \\[\n     61 \\text{ (initial apps)} - 9 \\text{ (deleted apps)} = 52 \\text{ (remaining apps)}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Download New Apps:**\n   - Travis downloaded **18 new apps**.\n   - To find out the total number of apps now:\n     \\[\n     52 \\text{ (remaining apps)} + 18 \\text{ (downloaded apps)} = 70 \\text{ (total apps)}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Final Answer:**\n   - After deleting and downloading apps, Travis has **70 apps** on his tablet.\n\n---\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{70}", "pred_ans": "70", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Travis had 61 apps on his tablet. He deleted 9 apps he didn't use anymore and downloaded 18 more. How many apps are on his tablet now?\n Solutio