 anything, so it's just about the flour. So, yeah, I think that's the correct answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nCarla will need \\boxed{6} cups of flour today and \\boxed{5} cups of flour tomorrow.\n</think>\n\nFirst, we determine the amount of flour needed per cookie. Since two cups of flour are needed to make a dozen cookies (12 cookies), we calculate the flour per cookie as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Flour per cookie} = \\frac{2 \\text{ cups}}{12 \\text{ cookies}} = \\frac{1}{6} \\text{ cups per cookie}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the flour needed for 36 cookies today:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Flour needed today} = 36 \\text{ cookies} \\times \\frac{1}{6} \\text{ cups per cookie} = 6 \\text{ cups}\n\\]\n\nThen, we calculate the flour needed for 30 cookies tomorrow:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Flour needed tomorrow} = 30 \\text{ cookies} \\times \\frac{1}{6} \\text{ cups per cookie} = 5 \\text{ cups}\n\\]\n\nWe can also verify this by calculating the number of dozens of cookies and then multiplying by the flour needed per dozen:\n\n- For 36 cookies today:\n  \\[\n  \\frac{36}{12} = 3 \\text{ dozens}\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  3 \\text{ dozens} \\times 2 \\text{ cups per dozen} = 6 \\text{ cups}\n  \\]\n\n- For 30 cookies tomorrow:\n  \\[\n  \\frac{30}{12} = 2.5 \\text{ dozens}\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  2.5 \\text{ dozens} \\times 2 \\text{ cups per dozen} = 5 \\text{ cups}\n  \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm the same results. Therefore, Carla will need \\boxed{6} cups of flour today and \\boxed{5} cups of flour tomorrow.", "pred_ans": "5", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Two cups of flour are needed to make a dozen cookies. Carla is making 36 cookies today and 30 cookies tomorrow. How many cups of flour will Carla need to bake the cookies today and tomorrow?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
