 bought a total of \\(\\boxed{112}\\) colors of crayons.", "pred_ans": "112", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Beatrice bought ten packets of crayons for her Art class. Six of the packets had eight pieces of colors each, and the other four packets had sixteen pieces of colors each. How many colors of crayons did Beatrice buy in all?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
{"question": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Bobby takes a 30 min lunch and 2 15 minutes break per day at the office.  After 5 days, how many hours do his lunches and breaks add up to?\n Solution:\n<think>\n", "gold_ans": "5", "rationale": "First, calculate the total lunch time Bobby takes over 5 days. He takes a 30-minute lunch each day. So, for 5 days, that's 5 multiplied by 0.5 hours, which equals 2.5 hours.\n\nNext, calculate the total break time Bobby takes over the same period. He takes 2 breaks of 15 minutes each day. So, that's 2 multiplied by 0.25 hours, which equals 0.5 hours.\n\nFinally, add the total lunch time and total break time together. 2.5 hours plus 0.5 hours equals 3 hours. So, Bobby's lunches and breaks add up to 3 hours over 5 days.\n</think>\n\nSure, let's solve the problem step by step.\n\n**Problem:**\nBobby takes a 30-minute lunch and 2 15-minute breaks per day at the office. After 5 days, how many hours do his lunches and breaks add up to?\n\n**Solution:**\n\n1. **Calculate the total lunch time over 5 days:**\n   \n   - **Lunch time per day:** 30 minutes\n   \n   - **Number of days:** 5\n   \n   - **Total lunch time:** \n     \\[\n     30 \\text{ minutes/day} \\times 5 \\text{ days} = 150 \\text{ minutes}\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Convert minutes to hours:**\n     \\[\n     150 \\text{ minutes} \\div 60 = 2.5 \\text{ hours}\n     \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the total break time over 5 days:**\n   \n   - **Breaks per day:** 2 \u00d7 15 minutes = 30 minutes\n   \n   - **Number of days:** 5\n   \n   - **Total break time:** \n     \\[\n     30 \\text{ minutes/day} \\times 5 \\text{ days} = 150 \\text{ minutes}\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Convert minutes to hours:**\n     \\[\n     150 \\text{ minutes} \\div 60 = 2.5 \\text{ hours}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Add the total lunch time and break time:**\n   \n   \\[\n   2.5 \\text{ hours (lunch)} + 2.5 \\text{ hours (breaks)} = 5 \\text{ hours}\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{5}\n\\]", "pred_ans": "5", "wrap_que": "Solve this math problem step by step. You MUST put your final answer in \\boxed{}. Problem: Bobby takes a 30 min lunch and 2 15 minutes break per day at the office.  After 5 days, how many hours do his lunches and breaks add up to?\n Solution:\n<think>\n"}
